    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "junior-qa-engineer-berlin-439004" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-20"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "We are Progyny Global, part of the Progyny, Inc. the leading fertility and family-building benefits provider in the US. Our shared mission? To make fertility and family-forming care accessible everywhere, breaking down barriers so that anyone can start a family, no matter where they are. With Progyny’s support, we're set to amplify our impact globally, reaching more individuals and families than ever before. Come and join us for a diverse and inclusive workplace and use “Tech for Good”! As a Junior QA Engineer, you’ll support software quality through both manual and automated testing. You will work closely with Product Managers, Frontend and Backend Engineers, Designers, and other QA colleagues to test new implementations and improve our testing processes. Our product includes different systems and integrations working together, so curiosity, communication, and a willingness to learn are important. You won’t be expected to know everything from day one, but we’re looking for someone who can gradually take more ownership as they learn the product and our processes. Tasks Manually test new features, bug fixes, and existing product flows. Create and execute clear test cases. Write and maintain automated tests using Playwright. Report, track, and retest bugs using Jira. Review user stories and raise questions when requirements are unclear. Collaborate with Developers and Product Managers throughout the testing process. Support test automation within our GitHub Actions workflows. Learn how different product areas and third-party integrations work together. Explore how AI tools can support testing, documentation, and automation. Requirements Some practical experience with manual software testing, through work, an internship, training, or personal projects. Basic experience with Playwright or another automation tool such as Cypress or Selenium. Basic knowledge of test case creation and bug reporting. Familiarity with Jira or a similar bug-tracking tool. Experience working in, or a good understanding of, an Agile environment. Good communication skills and confidence asking questions when something is unclear. Willingness to learn new tools, technologies, and product processes. It would be nice if you had: Basic JavaScript, TypeScript, or Python knowledge. Basic experience with Git and GitHub. API testing experience using Postman or a similar tool. Basic SQL or CI/CD knowledge. Experience using AI tools as part of your work or learning. Benefits 💰 Annual gross base salary range: €43000-48000/ year. 🎯 Bonus program & company equity. 👶 Fertility & family-building benefits: Access to Progyny Global Platform + €5,000 benefits budget. 🧘 Mental health support: 1:1 psychologist sessions & wellness tools via Spring Health. 🚲 Sustainable mobility benefit: Dance e-bike subscription or BVG public transport ticket. 🏡 Hybrid work: Up to 2 days per week from home. ✈️ Remote work: Up to 8 weeks per year. We believe in equal opportunities. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. 🚀 Ready to shape the future of quality assurance at Progyny Global? Apply now! Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "entry" ;
    schema:hiringOrganization kgjd:employer-progyny-global ;
