<https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/live/job/arbeitnow-manager-customer-success-london-209206> a prov:Entity,
        schema:JobPosting ;
    dcterms:source <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/source/arbeitnow> ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-20T20:33:44+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/creatoriq/manager-customer-success-london-209206> ;
    kgjobs:active true ;
    kgjobs:canonicalFingerprint "6da053f65820441e67f0bc70a5967473fe2c77daed4ce5db18bbcc63a247bf24" ;
    kgjobs:classification "not_match" ;
    kgjobs:firstSeenAt "2026-08-20T18:46:07+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:lastSeenAt "2026-08-20T20:33:44+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "manager-customer-success-london-209206" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-20"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "CreatorIQ is the operating system for creator-led growth trusted by more than 1,300 global brands and agencies. We’re on a mission to make businesses more human, and humans more impactful. We operate by our values — be intentional, pursue excellence every day, embrace the journey together, and be a good human — every day. CreatorIQ has earned the title of best companies to work for in multiple programs, including BuiltIn LA and NY. It’s been named a Fastest-Growing Company in North America on the Deloitte Technology Fast 500™ for four years, was named a leader in IDC MarketScape: Worldwide Influencer Marketing Platforms for Large Enterprises in 2025, was named a Leader by The Forrester New Wave™: Influencer Marketing Solutions, and has been consistently recognized by G2 as a Leader, and is rated 5 stars on Influencer MarketingHub. We operate in a flexible work model that combines both in-person and remote work to boost collaboration, enhance innovation, and adapt to individual work styles. We're seeking passionate, innovative minds to join our journey. Be a part of our dynamic team and let's transform the industry together! Manager, Customer Success As our EMEA Customer Success organization continues to grow, we're looking for an experienced, people-first leader to help scale a high-performing team and drive exceptional customer outcomes. As Manager, Customer Success, you'll lead a team of Customer Success Professionals responsible for helping enterprise customers maximize the value of the CreatorIQ platform. You'll empower your team through coaching, mentorship, and strategic leadership while ensuring exceptional customer experiences, strong retention outcomes, and operational excellence. You'll partner closely with Sales, Product, Professional Services, and Support teams to drive customer success at scale, champion AI-powered efficiencies, and foster a culture of accountability, collaboration, and continuous improvement. Location: London, UK (Hybrid, 3 days per week in office) Travel: Approximately 20% travel across EMEA customer locations. In this role, you’ll get to: Lead, coach, and develop a team of approximately 5-6 Customer Success Professionals, fostering a high-performance and customer-centric culture. Partner with team members on strategic customer engagements, executive business reviews, renewal discussions, and complex customer escalations. Drive retention, adoption, and growth outcomes by helping customers achieve measurable business value from the CreatorIQ platform. Own team forecasting, risk management, account health reviews, and operational processes to ensure consistent execution and visibility across the customer lifecycle. Collaborate cross-functionally with Sales, Product, Professional Services, and Support teams while identifying opportunities to leverage AI and automation to improve team productivity and customer outcomes. Who you are and what you’ll need for this position: 5+ years of experience in Enterprise Customer Success, Account Management, or a related customer-facing SaaS role, with previous people leadership experience. Proven ability to coach, mentor, and develop Customer Success professionals while building trust and driving team performance. Experience managing enterprise customer relationships, leading executive-level conversations, and partnering with senior stakeholders across complex organizations. Demonstrated success driving customer adoption, retention, renewals, and expansion, with strong commercial acumen and a customer-first mindset. Experience managing customer escalations and collaborating effectively across Sales, Product, Professional Services, and Support teams. Proficiency with CRM platforms (Salesforce preferred) and strong operational skills related to forecasting, pipeline management, and risk mitigation. Excellent communication, presentation, and stakeholder management skills. Experience within the influencer marketing, creator economy, social media technology, MarTech, or adjacent SaaS industries is strongly preferred. Comfortable leveraging AI tools to drive productivity, generate customer insights, and improve team effectiveness. Confidence can sometimes hold us back from applying for a job. But we'll let you in on a secret: there's no such thing as a 'perfect' candidate. Have 50% of the criteria? Excited about this opportunity? Passionate about what we do at CreatorIQ? Please apply! CreatorIQ is a place where everyone can grow. What you will get from us: People: work with talented, collaborative, and friendly people who love what they do. Guidance: utilize our learning platform to fully get the training and tools you’ll need to become successful here from your first day with us. Work/life harmony: 25 days vacation, floating and set holidays, wellness allowance, and paid parental leave. Stock options as part of our equity-sharing program. Healthcare coverage, encompassing mental health, physical therapies, dental, vision, cancer coverage, and more. Comprehensive perks program providing stipends for wellness, cell phone and internet, home office setup, mental wellness, professional development, plus occasional company-funded meal opportunities throughout the year. Who we are: CreatorIQ is the operating system for creator-led growth. Trusted by more than 1,300 global brands and agencies—including Burson, Delta Air Lines, Google, LVMH, Nestlé, and Sephora—CreatorIQ unifies creator marketing across paid, owned, earned, commerce, and community into one seamless, enterprise-grade ecosystem. With industry-leading intelligence infrastructure, rigorous compliance and security standards, and integrations with Meta, Snapchat, TikTok, YouTube, and more, CreatorIQ empowers brands and agencies to harness the creator economy as a strategic growth engine. CreatorIQ is a global company headquartered in Los Angeles with offices in Austin, New York, San Francisco, London, Manila, and Warsaw. Learn more at www.creatoriq.com and follow us on LinkedIn and Instagram. At CreatorIQ, we believe that diversity is the key to unlocking our full potential. We are committed to fostering an inclusive, equitable, and empowering work environment where everyone can thrive, regardless of race, ethnicity, gender, sexual orientation, age, religion, disability, or any other characteristic that makes us unique. By embracing our core values of being intentional, pursuing excellence every day, embracing the journey together, being a good human, and staying focused on what’s important, we create an atmosphere that promotes collaboration and growth. Join us to celebrate differences, innovate together, and be a part of a business that is disrupting the marketing industry. Compensation, Benefits and Beyond: We understand that a comprehensive benefits package plays a significant role in your overall compensation. To gain more insight into the various components of our total compensation, we invite you to review our benefits and perks. AI Transparency Notice We may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to support parts of the hiring process, such as reviewing applications and note taking during interviews. These tools assist our recruitment team but do not replace human judgment. Final hiring decisions are ultimately made by humans. If you would like more information about how your data is processed, please refer to our Global Candidate Privacy Notice. Compensation: £80K – £105K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus • £80K – £105K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Full Time" ;
    schema:hiringOrganization kgjd:employer-creatoriq ;
