    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "partnership-account-manager-uk-london-125510" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-20"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "About fonio We grew from $1M to $10M ARR in under 12 months and now serve 10,000+ customers. Fonio is Europe’s market leader for AI phone agents for SMBs. Now we’re expanding globally and into new products. We move fast, take ownership, give direct feedback, and avoid politics and unnecessary meetings. Join one of Europe’s fastest-growing companies. Your Role As Partner Manager UK you own the British and Irish partner channel end to end. Acquisition, activation, and enablement are all yours. You bring new partners in, you get them to their first closed deal, and you give them the resources they need to sell fonio on their own. You handle the full partner base in your market, except the strategic accounts. This is not desk based partner management. You sell alongside your partners, you sit in their customer calls, and you build the playbooks and materials that make them independent. What you will own Acquisition: You identify and screen potential partners across the UK and Ireland. You assess their real potential and decide how each one gets handled. Activation: You get partners to their first joint closed deal. You run the sales calls yourself so the partner sees a strong sales process live and learns from it. You join larger customer negotiations. Enablement: You teach partners how to sell fonio. You build and provide the resources they need, from pitch material to objection handling, and you are their go to contact for questions. Account Management: Regular check ins with your partners, unlocking upsell potential in their existing customer base, and opening new customers through and for your partners. Your targets and KPIs Revenue through partners Number of qualified partners per quarter Number of activated partners (first joint deal closed) Activation rate and repeat activation rate Upsell rate in the existing base Who we are looking for Languages: English native is a must. German, French, Italian, or Spanish are a plus. Sales background, ideally you have walked the SDR to AE path yourself. Channel or partner experience is an advantage. Hands on closer mentality. You sell yourself and train partners at the same time. Strong self discipline, a real sense of ownership, and genuine drive to prove yourself. You are up for the Vienna start and the move to London afterwards, and you are willing to travel for partner visits and larger customer negotiations on site. Hiring Process 15 min intro 45 min skill interview & case study with David 20 min Deep dive with our CCO Alex 20 min culture fit with both founders Compensation: £70K – £120K • Offers Equity • £70K – £120K • Offers Equity Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Full Time" ;
    schema:hiringOrganization kgjd:employer-fonio ;
    schema:identifier "arbeitnow-partnership-account-manager-uk-london-125510" ;
    schema:jobLocation [ a schema:Place ;
            schema:name "London" ] ;
    schema:title "Partnership Account Manager UK" ;
    schema:url <https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/fonio/partnership-account-manager-uk-london-125510> .

<https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/live/job/arbeitnow-people-operations-coordinator-london-31892> a prov:Entity,
        schema:JobPosting ;
    dcterms:source <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/source/arbeitnow> ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-20T20:33:44+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/lemfi/people-operations-coordinator-london-31892> ;
    kgjobs:active true ;
    kgjobs:canonicalFingerprint "0aefe3ed3a4c8c3d1383c814d8cc92c964b19ff1263db3a8380e3c7d0e608f26" ;
    kgjobs:classification "not_match" ;
    kgjobs:firstSeenAt "2026-08-20T18:46:07+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:lastSeenAt "2026-08-20T20:33:44+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "people-operations-coordinator-london-31892" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-20"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "LemFi (Series B) is building the go-to financial app for the Global South. Moving to a new country shouldn’t mean starting from zero. That's why our team of 400+ spanning 20+ countries is building a financial ecosystem that helps immigrants stay connected to home, build stability, and create wealth regardless of where they are from or where they live. What began as fast, affordable remittances is now evolving into a complete platform for multi-currency accounts, payments, credit, and long-term financial growth. With millions of users across the globe, we process over $1B in monthly transactions to 30+ countries, proving that borders shouldn't limit financial opportunity. About the role As People Operations Coordinator, you'll be the backbone of global people operations - the person who keeps core processes running smoothly, is the go-to for employee questions and ensures we stay compliant across every market we operate in. This is a broad, hands-on role in a global, fast-changing business. You'll be building and running processes designed to scale as we grow, not just maintaining what already exists, and you'll need to be comfortable with pace, ambiguity, and having your attention split across a lot of moving parts at once. What you’ll build and own Core operations: Own core people operations processes including onboarding, offboarding, contracts, probation management, background checks, right-to-work, and leave and absence management. HRIS data: Own our HRIS data integrity, maintain accurate records, run audits, build out workflows and automations that reduce manual data entry and admin as we scale. Benefits administration: Manage enrolment, changes, and employee queries across benefits programmes. AI integration: Own and maintain content for our AI HR bot so employees get fast, accurate self-serve answers, and act as our champion for identifying new ways AI tools can support the people function. Employee and first-line manager support: Be the go-to for employee questions, manage our jira ticketing system Ad-hoc projects: Support on People related projects, there’s a new HRIS implementation coming (amongst many other initiatives)! People metrics and reporting: Produce reporting that gives the business visibility into what's working and what needs attention. Your experience 2+ years in a people operations or HR generalist roles, ideally spanning multiple countries Comfortable operating in a fast-paced, ever-changing environment, juggling multiple workstreams at once Experience improving or automating a process, with an eye toward building for scale Proficiency with modern HRIS platforms and comfort maintaining accurate, structured data Nice to have Experience in a high-growth, multi-country startup environment Experience supporting an HRIS implementation or migration Why Join LemFi? Love shouldn’t be expensive, yet those working hardest for their families often face predatory fees and banking exclusion. We're changing this. At LemFi, you won’t be just a cog in a machine. Whether designing products, scaling operations, or telling our story, you’ll tackle complex challenges with real, immediate impact. Your work goes beyond metrics - it puts money back in families’ pockets and offers access to the previously excluded. Join us to make a meaningful difference, where high performance is a lifeline for millions. You can connect with us on LinkedIn and Instagram and if you haven't already, download the app on the App Store or Google Play. Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Full Time" ;
    schema:hiringOrganization kgjd:employer-lemfi ;
    schema:identifier "arbeitnow-people-operations-coordinator-london-31892" ;
