    schema:datePosted "2026-08-20"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "At Jellyfish, we believe in the power of diverse perspectives and inclusive collaboration. We welcome individuals who excel in collaborative, varied teams and value the unique contributions that each person brings to the table. Jellyfish is a global digital marketing agency; a unique fusion of tech enthusiasts, creative minds, and media and data experts all united to empower our clients along their digital journey. Our commitment to embracing diverse perspectives fuels our innovation and strategies that challenge the status quo, reinvent media activation, and craft influential stories for our global clients and their customers. Join us in shaping a future where business growth and personal fulfilment go hand in hand. Capability Overview In Jellyfish Creative, we embed Gen AI at our core to create, adapt, connect and optimise award-winning content at scale. In 150+ markets. For the world’s leading brands. Our creative model combines tech-driven ideation with human-generated social creativity, connecting all 400 creative and experienced experts across the globe, powered by the integration of Pencil Pro. AI Studios is where creative talent supercharges Jellyfish’s market-leading experience in content, production, transcreation and localisation generating content at scale and our most dynamic, diverse, and inspiring talent forms the award-winning Creative Collective, focusing on human-generated social creative with cultural relevance that can live on any platform or medium. Creating end-to-end solutions that bring audience expectations and platform algorithms together with relevance, clarity and cultural resonance. Job Description As a Senior Design Manager, you’ll be responsible for leading and managing the design process on client projects, ensuring briefs are accurately understood and executed. Working closely with your Project Manager and Senior Design Capability Support, you'll help streamline workflows and elevate the quality of the design work produced. This role provides the opportunity to contribute to both the creation of impactful assets and the development of the design community at Jellyfish, all while focusing on continuous growth and excellence. You’ll be a key player in delivering high-quality design assets, including static and animated digital content for social media, and will have the opportunity to foster innovation within a global team. By embracing both creative and technical processes, you’ll help ensure smooth project onboarding and contribute to the team’s overall success. Additionally, you’ll have the opportunity to leverage the AI platform Pencil Pro, enhancing your design process and helping to generate even more effective, data-driven creative assets. The salary range for this position is between £50,000-60,000 GBP, annually, and final offer is based upon experience. This is a hybrid position based out of our London office. Responsibilities Create a diverse range of digital and print design assets, focusing on social media content, including both static and animated designs. Utilize design software like Figma and the Adobe Creative Suite (Photoshop, Illustrator, After Effects) to produce high-quality assets. Understand and apply interactive design principles, ensuring engaging and user-friendly outcomes. Demonstrate proficiency in Motion Graphics and Video Editing, utilizing tools such as Adobe After Effects and Premiere Pro. Leverage knowledge of HTML, CSS, and JavaScript to effectively communicate with development teams and understand technical possibilities. Stay current with the latest digital design trends, AI tools like ChatGPT, and integrate them into your design process to enhance creative output. Leverage the AI platform Pencil Pro to streamline your creative workflow, generating optimized designs based on data and client insights. Align closely with Project Managers and the creative team to promptly receive and develop project briefs. Actively participate in project kick-off meetings and review all relevant project materials to ensure understanding of scope and objectives. Understand project timelines and deadlines, ensuring deliverables are completed on schedule. Interrogate briefs and ask for clarification on any required materials or project details to avoid miscommunication. Ensure project scope, role, and hours are well-understood and accurately tracked in Financial Force. Demonstrate a proactive approach by asking questions and seeking clarification when necessary. Actively participate in internal and external meetings, maintaining clear communication with team members and clients. Respond to feedback and concerns from clients and colleagues in a professional, constructive manner. Participate in collaborative activities and communication channels with the broader project and capability teams. Qualifications Advanced proficiency in English. 5+ of experience in a senior design role, preferably within an agency or similar environment. Ability to follow design processes, confidentiality protocols, and file organization standards. Strong innovative thinking and problem-solving skills, contributing valuable insights during brainstorming sessions. Expertise in design tools like Figma and Adobe Creative Suite (Photoshop, InDesign Illustrator and After Effects). Solid understanding of design principles and typography, with the ability to create effective layouts, ensuring sharp attention to detail across various channels. Knowledgeable about digital design principles and how to apply them across multiple formats and platforms. Familiar with brand guidelines and experienced in adapting them across various projects. Strong ability to combine speed and technique to produce high-quality assets efficiently, even at scale. Creative problem solver with the ability to contribute strategically and think outside the box. Skilled in quality control (QC) for your own work and understanding project workflows to ensure smooth delivery. Up-to-date with the latest design trends, techniques, and emerging technologies. Able to export and optimize assets to meet platform specifications and best practices, ensuring file size and naming conventions are followed. Capable of annotating files and providing supporting documentation when necessary. Unafraid to raise concerns and suggest improvements to the team, particularly if issues arise during the project or process Note: We emphasise skills, expertise and behavioural attributes over years of experience and traditional degrees. If you want to join our collaborative team, we invite you to apply today with your resume in English. Additional Information Join Jellyfish and experience a workplace where we prioritise your growth, celebrate your contributions, and empower you to tailor your work environment to suit your needs. 💰 Reward: You'll be eligible to join our discretionary annual bonus scheme. 💫 Custom Work Environment: Work remotely for up to 60% of your days and shape your day between 8am. and 6:30pm with flexible working hours. 👪 Family Support: Enjoy 14 weeks of paid leave for primary caregivers and 4 weeks of paid leave for secondary caregivers. We also provide £1000 (or equivalent) towards courses for returning primary caregivers to support your transition back into work. Unfortunately, there has been an increase in fake recruiters impersonating Jellyfish and unlawfully using our brand name. If you are unsure if an email with a job offer you have received is genuinely from Jellyfish, or if you suspect any fraudulent activity, please report it to Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
