    schema:description "<div class=\"content-intro\"><p><span class=\"TextRun SCXW142035299 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"auto\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW142035299 BCX0\">Resolve to Save Lives (RTSL)</span></span><span data-contrast=\"none\"> is a global health organization that partners locally and globally to create and scale solutions to the world’s deadliest </span><span data-contrast=\"none\">health threats. </span><span data-contrast=\"none\">Millions of people die from preventable health threats. We collaborate to close the gap between proven, life-saving solutions and the people who need them. </span><span data-contrast=\"none\">Since 2017, </span><span data-contrast=\"none\">we’ve</span><span data-contrast=\"none\"> worked with governments and other partners in more than 60 countries to save millions of lives. We work toward a future where people live</span> <span data-contrast=\"none\">longer, healthier lives, communities flourish, and economies thrive. This is an ambitious vision, and it inspires us and our partners to make progress every day.</span><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">&nbsp;</span></p></div><p><strong><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Position Purpose</span></strong><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">&nbsp;</span></p> <p><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\"><span data-contrast=\"auto\"><span class=\"TextRun SCXW72428673 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"none\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW72428673 BCX0\">Reporting to the Chief Development Officer (CDO), the <strong>Senior Manager, Development</strong> owns and grows a portfolio of foundation and philanthropic funders</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW72428673 BCX0\"> and prospects</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW72428673 BCX0\">. The Senior Manager carries each relationship </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW72428673 BCX0\">across the full funding lifecycle -</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW72428673 BCX0\">-</span> <span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW72428673 BCX0\">from identification </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW72428673 BCX0\">and</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW72428673 BCX0\"> cultivation </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW72428673 BCX0\">through solicitation, award, reporting</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW72428673 BCX0\">,</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW72428673 BCX0\"> renewal, </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW72428673 BCX0\">and growth -- </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW72428673 BCX0\">and is accountable for </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW72428673 BCX0\">delivering portfolio goals</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW72428673 BCX0\">. </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW72428673 BCX0\">T</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW72428673 BCX0\">he Senior Manager will deepen </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW72428673 BCX0\">existing </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW72428673 BCX0\">relationships and bring new funders to the organization. </span></span><span class=\"TextRun SCXW72428673 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"auto\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW72428673 BCX0\">The role combines relationship management, business development, proposal leadership, and cross-functional coordination, working closely with program, finance, communications, and legal colleagues to translate RTSL’s priorities into compelling</span> <span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW72428673 BCX0\">funding opportunities.</span></span></span>&nbsp;</span></p> <p><strong><span data-contrast=\"auto\">Core Duties and Responsibilities</span></strong><span data-ccp-props=\"{}\">&nbsp;</span></p> <p><em><strong>Portfolio management</strong></em>&nbsp;</p> <ul> <li>Own a portfolio of foundation and philanthropic funders and prospects, carrying each relationship from identification and qualification through cultivation, solicitation, award and renewal.</li> <li>Develop and execute annual engagement plans for significant relationships and prospects in the portfolio, with clear objectives for cultivation, solicitation, renewal, and growth.</li> <li>Serve as a key point of contact for assigned funders and prospects, building trusted relationships with program officers and other decision-makers at funding organizations.&nbsp;</li> <li>Research and qualify new funding prospects that fit RTSL's priorities and move them into the pipeline.&nbsp;</li> <li>Monitor portfolio performance and pipeline progress against annual revenue and relationship goals, adjusting engagement approaches as needed.&nbsp;</li> </ul> <p><em><strong>Proposals, reporting and compliance</strong></em>&nbsp;</p> <ul> <li>Lead complex proposal and concept note development from opportunity assessment through submission, establishing timelines, coordinating cross-functional inputs, and ensuring a compelling and coherent final product.&nbsp;</li> <li>Work with internal stakeholders to shape value propositions that position RTSL's priorities for funding.&nbsp;</li> <li>Ensure high-quality, timely reporting and full compliance with grant terms across the portfolio.&nbsp;</li> <li>Coordinate the development, review, and execution of grant agreements, Memoranda of Understanding, and other partnership documentation in collaboration with legal and other relevant internal teams.&nbsp;</li> </ul> <p><em><strong>Representation and external engagement</strong></em>&nbsp;</p> <ul> <li>Represent RTSL with funders and at key events and conferences, communicating the organization's mission, strategy and results.&nbsp;</li> <li>Coordinate donor field visits, joint communications and public acknowledgments with the Communications team.&nbsp;</li> </ul> <p><em><strong>Processes, tools and platforms</strong></em>&nbsp;</p> <ul> <li>Maintain disciplined use of the pipeline tracker and Monday.com so that pipeline progress and follow-up stay accurate and visible.&nbsp;</li> <li>Follow RTSL's development standard operating procedures and help keep the team's processes, tools and platforms up to date.&nbsp;<strong>&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;</li> </ul> <p><em><strong>Required Qualifications:</strong></em></p> <p><em><strong>Education:</strong></em> &nbsp;</p> <ul> <li>Bachelor's degree in a relevant field (e.g., public health, international development, nonprofit management, communications, business); advanced degree is a plus.&nbsp;</li> </ul> <p><em><strong>Experience:</strong></em>&nbsp;</p> <ul> <li>Minimum 8 years' experience in fundraising, development, or resource mobilization, with a demonstrated track record of contributing substantially to the cultivation and securing of significant philanthropic awards, including six and seven figure funding.&nbsp;</li> <li>Direct experience managing foundation and philanthropic relationships end to end, including proposal development, reporting and renewal.&nbsp;</li> <li>Experience in global health, international development, or a comparable mission-driven organization.&nbsp;</li> </ul> <p><em><strong>Skills &amp; abilities:</strong></em>&nbsp;</p> <ul> <li>Strong relationship manager, able to build trust with funders and hold a portfolio independently.&nbsp;</li> <li>Excellent written and verbal communication, with the ability to turn technical program content into a compelling case for support.&nbsp;</li> <li>Structured, organized, and persistent, with strong project management skills and the ability to take complex efforts across the finish line.&nbsp;</li> <li>Strong influencing and collaboration skills, with the ability to mobilize colleagues across functions and levels around funding opportunities, deadlines, and donor commitments.&nbsp;</li> <li>Collaborative and flexible team player who contributes to a harmonious and productive work environment.&nbsp;</li> <li>Comfortable and able to operate well in a fast-paced, remote, mission-driven environment.&nbsp;</li> <li>Passionate about global health.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li> </ul> <p><strong>Compensation and Benefits:</strong></p> <p>Resolve to Save Lives prides itself on cultivating a supportive, connected remote team doing work that matters. We do everything possible to ensure our employees are connected and set up for success. &nbsp;</p> <p>The starting salary range for this position in the US is $105,000 to $120,000 annually. The exact offer will be determined by various factors, such as the candidate's skills and experience relative to the requirements of the role. For applicants based outside the US, salaries are set according to national labor rates for the international NGO sector.</p> <p>In addition to a competitive salary, Resolve to Save Lives provides a generous package of benefits, including: &nbsp;&nbsp;</p> <ul> <li>Health insurance for you and your dependents &nbsp;</li> <li>Contributions toward retirement &nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>Paid annual leave and sick leave, in addition to public holidays &nbsp;</li> <li>Two paid, week-long organization-wide breaks at mid-year and end-of-year &nbsp;&nbsp;</li> <li>Professional development and home office setup benefits &nbsp;</li> <li>Up-to-date computer equipment <span data-ccp-props=\"{&quot;134233117&quot;:false,&quot;134233118&quot;:false,&quot;335551550&quot;:0,&quot;335551620&quot;:0,&quot;335559738&quot;:240,&quot;335559739&quot;:240}\">&nbsp;</span></li> </ul><div class=\"content-conclusion\"><p><span class=\"TextRun SCXW71186963 BCX0\" lang=\"EN-US\" data-contrast=\"auto\"><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW71186963 BCX0\">RTSL believes its programs are strengthened when they are developed and supported by individuals with diverse life experiences whose understanding of social and cultural issues can help make our work and workforce more inclusive. We encourage applications from and </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW71186963 BCX0\">provide</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW71186963 BCX0\"> equal employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, ancestry, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability, marital status, organ donor status, or status as a veteran. Resolve to Save Lives </span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW71186963 BCX0\">complies with</span><span class=\"NormalTextRun SCXW71186963 BCX0\"> all applicable US EEO laws.</span></span><span class=\"EOP SCXW71186963 BCX0\" data-ccp-props=\"{}\">&nbsp;</span></p></div> Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:hiringOrganization kgjd:employer-resolvetosavelives ;
    schema:identifier "arbeitnow-senior-manager-development-remote-us-or-uk-109670" ;
    schema:title "Senior Manager, Development (Remote - US or UK)" ;
    schema:url <https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/resolvetosavelives/senior-manager-development-remote-us-or-uk-109670> .

<https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/live/job/arbeitnow-senior-marketing-manager-in-vollzeit-hamburg-230510> a prov:Entity,
